WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.920
The children spent many sunny days at the lagoon.

2
00:00:03.921 --> 00:00:07.061
This was where the mermaids lived and played.

3
00:00:07.062 --> 00:00:10.959
Wendy was fascinated by the mermaids and wanted to meet them.

4
00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:14.938
But the only human they would talk to was Peter.

5
00:00:14.939 --> 00:00:18.706
Sometimes they even let him sit on their tails.

6
00:00:18.707 --> 00:00:23.248
When they saw Wendy, however, they would dive back into the water.

7
00:00:23.249 --> 00:00:26.343
Then they would use their tails to splash her.

8
00:00:26.344 --> 00:00:29.637
So Wendy had to watch from a distance.

9
00:00:29.638 --> 00:00:34.348
The best time to see mermaids was on sunny days after a rain.

10
00:00:34.349 --> 00:00:38.503
Then they surfaced in large numbers to play with their bubbles.

11
00:00:38.504 --> 00:00:41.350
The bubbles were made of rainbow water.

12
00:00:41.351 --> 00:00:47.317
The mermaids hit the colorful bubbles from one to another with their fins until the bubbles burst.

13
00:00:47.318 --> 00:00:49.687
It was lovely to watch.

14
00:00:49.688 --> 00:00:52.992
Sometimes the children came to the lagoon.

15
00:00:52.993 --> 00:00:56.706
They would sit on Marooners' Rock to have a picnic lunch.

16
00:00:56.707 --> 00:01:03.328
First, they would eat, and then Wendy would insist they rest for half an hour before swimming.

17
00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:07.632
Obediently, they would lie down on the rock in the sunlight.

18
00:01:07.633 --> 00:01:12.852
Watching over the children, Wendy would gaze at them with great pride.

19
00:01:12.853 --> 00:01:18.147
It was just such a day on Marooners' Rock when a great adventure occurred.

20
00:01:18.148 --> 00:01:22.718
They had all dozed off except for Wendy, who continued to sew.

21
00:01:22.719 --> 00:01:26.858
Suddenly a great change came over the lagoon.

22
00:01:26.859 --> 00:01:31.789
The sun disappeared, and a chilly breeze made stiff waves in the water.

23
00:01:31.790 --> 00:01:38.099
The surface of the rock became cold. Something frightening was coming.

24
00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:43.081
When Wendy saw the dark gloom rising, she should have awakened the boys.

25
00:01:43.082 --> 00:01:46.688
But being a new mother, she didn't know this.

26
00:01:46.689 --> 00:01:52.751
Instead, she thought it was more important to stick to her rule of a half hour's rest.

27
00:01:52.752 --> 00:01:58.541
Even when she heard the sound of oncoming oars, she let the boys sleep on.

28
00:01:58.542 --> 00:02:02.166
They all continued to sleep—except for Peter.

29
00:02:02.167 --> 00:02:06.944
When he heard the splash of oars, he sprang up with excitement.

30
00:02:06.945 --> 00:02:11.133
"Pirates coming—dive!" he yelled.

31
00:02:11.134 --> 00:02:14.876
Instantly, the children all dove into the water.

32
00:02:14.877 --> 00:02:18.786
The boys and Wendy swam quickly away.

33
00:02:18.787 --> 00:02:25.046
By the time the small pirate boat drew near, Marooners' Rock was deserted.

34
00:02:25.047 --> 00:02:31.162
Three figures stood up in the boat— the pirates Smee and Starkey, and Tiger Lily.

35
00:02:31.163 --> 00:02:35.671
The hands and feet of the Indian princess were tied with rope.

36
00:02:35.672 --> 00:02:39.530
The pirates' plan was to leave their captive on Marooners' Rock.

37
00:02:39.531 --> 00:02:45.395
For centuries, evil captains had tied sailors to the rock, waiting for the tide to rise.

38
00:02:45.396 --> 00:02:48.824
When the water rose, the men drowned.

39
00:02:48.825 --> 00:02:53.545
This was the fate the pirates planned for Tiger Lily too.

40
00:02:53.546 --> 00:02:59.079
Traveling in what was now almost darkness, the pirates crashed into the rock.

41
00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:03.492
"Lift the girl onto the rock!" Smee yelled.

42
00:03:03.493 --> 00:03:09.303
The proud Indian maiden did not resist but continued to hold her head high.

43
00:03:09.304 --> 00:03:15.630
Nearby, two heads bobbed up and down in the water. It was Peter and Wendy.

44
00:03:15.631 --> 00:03:19.174
Wendy wept at the sight of poor Tiger Lily.

45
00:03:19.175 --> 00:03:23.486
Peter was angered by the unfairness of two against one.

46
00:03:23.487 --> 00:03:30.290
Even though Tiger Lily had been an enemy of the boys, he now wanted to save her.

47
00:03:30.291 --> 00:03:37.616
Imitating the voice of Hook to perfection, Peter called out, "Ahoy, you pirates!"

48
00:03:37.617 --> 00:03:42.727
"It's Captain Hook," the pirates said to each other with surprise.

49
00:03:42.728 --> 00:03:48.290
"Captain, we have the Indian princess," they shouted.

50
00:03:48.291 --> 00:03:54.458
"Cut her ropes and set her free," commanded Peter in Captain Hook's voice.

51
00:03:54.459 --> 00:03:58.109
"But Captain . . ." they called back.

52
00:03:58.110 --> 00:04:06.149
"I said set her free at once or you'll tangle with my hook!" yelled Peter.

53
00:04:06.150 --> 00:04:11.474
"We'd better do what the captain orders," said Smee to Starkey.

54
00:04:11.475 --> 00:04:15.095
They cut the ropes on Tiger Lily's hands and feet.

55
00:04:15.096 --> 00:04:20.601
Immediately, she slipped gracefully into the water and swam away from sight.

56
00:04:20.602 --> 00:04:25.346
For a brief moment, there was complete silence in the lagoon.

57
00:04:25.347 --> 00:04:28.485
Wendy looked at Peter with great admiration.

58
00:04:28.486 --> 00:04:31.481
Peter tried really hard not to look pleased.

59
00:04:31.482 --> 00:04:34.660
The pirates struggled to get their boat off the rock.

60
00:04:34.661 --> 00:04:40.096
Suddenly a voice cried out, "Ahoy, you pirates!"

61
00:04:40.097 --> 00:04:50.333
It was the voice of the real Captain Hook, and he was in the water too!

